# Agent rules live only in AGENTS.md

The meta-repository root has no `CLAUDE.md`, `.claude/CLAUDE.md` or `CLAUDE.local.md`. Rules are written in `AGENTS.md`, which Claude Code and Codex read. Claude Code reads `AGENTS.md` natively since version 2.1.277 ([documentation](https://code.claude.com/docs/en/memory#agents-md)).

## Considered Options

**`CLAUDE.md` importing `@AGENTS.md`.** Works on any version, but adds a second file that can be forgotten when updating.

**A `CLAUDE.md` symlink to `AGENTS.md`.** Symlinks are awkward on Windows, and some tools refuse to write through a link.

**Only `AGENTS.md` (chosen).** One file, one place to edit.

## Consequences

- Claude Code 2.1.277 or newer is required.
- Any `CLAUDE.md`, `.claude/CLAUDE.md` or `CLAUDE.local.md` in the root or above turns off reading `AGENTS.md`. `mise run lint` catches such files in the root.
- A clone's `CLAUDE.md` lives below the root and does not turn reading off. The agent reads it before editing that clone, as `AGENTS.md` requires.
- Loading is checked with the `/context` command at the start of a session.
